WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468
-This is very exciting
that you're doing a tour.

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.136
It's been a long time since
you've been out on the road.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.504
-Seven years.
-Seven years. And this is nice.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.506 size:88% position:44%
The show is a little bit
about your upbringing,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
who you were
when you were young.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:10.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
And is this true? You were
a great lover of nature
from a very young age.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My first love.
Probably like 5, 6, 7,

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:16.149
I was out foraging and trying
to, you know, work things out.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:20.420 size:84% position:42%
[ Laughs ] I tell a lot
of stories in the show,

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.856
teal stories about me
and my family and my upbringing

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.225 line:92%
and the state of the world.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.726 line:92%
This one isn't in the show,

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that just
reminded me of one.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.162 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
When I was about --

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've got older brothers
and sisters, okay?

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:34.300
So when I was about 8, I got
two brothers and a sister.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
My sister,
she must have been about 20.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a big gap. 20 and 8.
-It is a big gap.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:43.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
In fact,
it goes 11, 13, 14...

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.612
I remember when I was about 12,
I asked my mum,

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:48.481
"Why are my brothers and sisters
so much older than me?"

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:51.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she just said,
"You were a mistake."

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.519 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:55.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of honesty.
Lots of honesty in my family.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.892 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So, I'm out,

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my sister and her husband
took me out in the woods.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:04.064
And I always loved finding
things and looking for lizards.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:09.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I found this perfect
shed snakeskin,

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:10.336 line:92%
and it was beautiful, right?

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:13.206
And I held up, and I realized
my sister was terrified of it.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.809
She was going, "Put it down.
Put it down. It's got germs."

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I started
chasing her with it,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she was going,
"Put it down."

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:19.779 line:92%
And she was sort of laughing.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You're not going to
come in the car, right?"

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.483 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So I left it there.

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:25.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then years later,
I was about 14.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had some friends around,
and I was teasing her.

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was saying to her --
Showing off.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:33.927
"Oh, I used to scare her. She
was terrified of a snakeskin."

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she chose
that moment to tell me

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
that actually
I had been running around

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.533 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
with a used condom.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:43.136 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.872 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.777 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I really --

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm so impressed
that she waited --

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, she really --
That's like a kill shot.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
She had it in her back pocket,
waiting.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Well, I suppose she thought --

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
She didn't want to talk about
what a condom was.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
But as I was winding her up,
she thought,

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No. Now's the time.
-Yeah.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:09.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
This -- You want to do this?
You want a piece of me?"

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.597 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This love of nature
has continued.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
You recently posted
these photos.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.902 line:92%
You saved a squirrel's life.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a little -- I would do
anything for animals.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:21.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
I found this little
baby squirrel.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:23.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was --
We live near a graveyard,

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:25.044
and he was out in the road
and he was sort of dazed,

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.514 size:78% position:39%
a little bit injured.
And I thought, "Aww."

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:28.281 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And he was so tiny.

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:31.184
And you can't -- You mustn't
really take them from the wild.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:35.088
And the RSPCA don't really care
for wild animals like that.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.624
They say, "Leave it there.
The parents might be around."

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:41.861
So I went and sat with it in the
graveyard for like two hours.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.297
My girlfriend ran home
and got some nuts, right,

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:47.033
which I was chewing up and
feeding it like a little pup

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.235 size:81% position:41%
because it was like --
And then we found --

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.804
On the Internet, we found
it liked strawberries.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we went and got
some strawberries.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And here you are
feeding it a strawberry.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A little strawberry.
It was --

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he went asleep
in my hood.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I didn't move,
and I was there --

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
And after about
three or four hours,

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:07.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
he sort of perked up and he
sort of jumped on the thing...

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was looking at me,
and we sort of left him.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:13.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
And probably eaten by a cat
straight after, but...

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:16.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know --
-Again, there's something --

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:19.899
If he got eaten by a cat,
he never had a better meal.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.434 line:92%
-Yeah. And nor did the cat.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.804 size:84% position:42%
The cat goes, "This one
tastes of strawberries!

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:27.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is amazing!
I want strawberries!"

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then the cat
was telling his cats,

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:32.078
"You know where squirrels
are great? The graveyard.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:34.080
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.
-You got to go to the graveyard.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have nutty,
strawberry squirrels."

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:38.518 size:81% position:41%
-I don't want to think
it was his last meal.

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause that sort of --
That always stresses me out.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, on, like, death row,
they give you a last meal.

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:45.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
They say, "What do you want
for the last meal?"

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.327
I'd say,
"I'm not hungry, to be honest."

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:49.896 size:88% position:44%
I mean, the stress of --
How could you enjoy it?

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:54.634
I'd say, "Are there nuts
in this? 'Cause that's...

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:57.337 line:92%
This is gluten-free, isn't it?"

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:59.339 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:00.707 line:92%
The funny thing is my whole life

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:04.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
people have told me you
have to chew your food more.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:05.311 line:92%
-Why? Do you eat like a dog?

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just swallow it?
What do you mean?

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:09.349
-Well, you know, you're supposed
to chew your food like 50 times.

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:11.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do, yeah. I know.
I gulp it down.

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:12.151 line:92%
-But that would be the meal

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I would just be
chewing the [bleep] out of it.

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:17.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just like...
-Yeah.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just really making it last.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think
that would work, though.

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
After a few days,
they'd probably go,

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:24.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You're making this last,
aren't you?"

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:29.335 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah. "This is more
than enough chewing."

